Issue 29 done, committed as `7a4b1fc`, outcome written.

**All four fixes landed** (in `engine/fleet.ts` and `engine/server.ts`):
1. Busy pinned ports now name the holder (` by pool <dir> (pid <pid>)`) from a live fleet-registry lookup by port; bare message preserved as fallback.
2. Pool lock claims atomically via O_EXCL; a live holder refuses, stale locks clear only after a re-read confirms, and failed-bind cleanup removes the pid file only when it still names our pid. This closes the review's TOCTOU window.
3. Fleet registry writes serialize through a `.lock` file (live-holder wait, stale-lock recovery) plus temp-file-and-rename, so concurrent different-pool boots lose no entry.
4. The em dash in the registration comment is a colon.

**Verification**: live two-pool and real-concurrent-process tests (new concurrency tests stable across repeated runs), 220 tests pass, `tsc --noEmit` clean, UI build clean. A two-axis code review ran; its one real finding (a null-null re-read race in the lock takeover) was fixed.

One pre-existing condition, documented in the Issue's Notes: `engine.test.ts`'s resolver-log rotation test flakes intermittently on base HEAD too (merge-resolver timing race, out of this Issue's scope). Left as found.
